{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the days of his weeping passed.</b> From here we learn that one must not mourn for the greatest in Israel more than thirty days, for it says ויעברו ימי בכיתו — and who do we have greater than Moshe? Yet they mourned him only thirty days, as it is written of him (Deuteronomy 34:8): ״ויתמו ימי בכי אבל משה״ — 'and the days of weeping and mourning for Moshe were ended.' And the Sages, of blessed memory, had been inclined to mourn for Rabbenu HaKadosh a full year, until they found this verse about Moshe: ויתמו ימי בכי אבל משה."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:52.506404573Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}